course: dictionary
lesson: 5089
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Intelligence is one of them. Most often it means the ability to learn, understand and think clearly. The words around it show you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: Read «AI means artificial intelligence: computer programs that do tasks like talking, sorting or answering.» The words computer programs tell you this is about machines, so intelligence here is the third meaning, not the first.
explain: Intelligence can also mean secret information gathered about enemies or dangers. Try each meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Intelligence means the ability to learn, understand and think clearly.
fact: Intelligence can also mean secret information gathered about enemies or dangers, and the people who gather it.
fact: In computers, artificial intelligence (AI) is a machine's ability to do tasks that seem to need thinking.
fact: «Artificial» means made by people, not grown by nature.
fact: Intelligence is a noun with no plural.
exercise: «AI means artificial intelligence: computer programs that do tasks like talking, sorting or answering.» In this sentence, what does intelligence mean? | Gathering food in the wild | Secret information about enemies | *A machine's ability to do tasks that seem to need thinking | Feeling tired after a long day
exercise: «Soldiers used military intelligence to find where the enemy camp was.» What does intelligence mean here? | A clever idea for a game | The ability to learn and think clearly | A test taken at school | *Secret information about enemies
exercise: «She used her intelligence to solve the puzzle.» Which meaning fits best? | Feeling hungry and sad | *The ability to learn, understand and think clearly | Secret information about enemies or dangers | A computer program that sorts and answers
test: What does artificial mean in «artificial intelligence»? | Kept secret | Very old | *Made by people, not grown by nature | Grown by nature
test: Which phrase tells someone to think hard and well? | the enemy's secret plans | military intelligence | artificial intelligence | *use your intelligence
exam: «The spy gathered intelligence about the enemy's plans.» Which meaning is used? | *Secret information about enemies or dangers | A computer program that sorts and answers | The ability to learn and think clearly | Feeling sad and tired
